# What scripts/check-personal-details.sh may find in the tracked tree of coldmail-verify (module 1) without going red: path-glob|literal|reason.
# Everything not listed here and not in an allowed class (documentation, private, loopback and other special-use ranges) is RED. The reason is mandatory; an entry that matches nothing is RED.
# The format and the rules are in the header of the gate (coldmail-platform/scripts/check-personal-details.sh). Built on 2026-11-17 from `git archive HEAD` of module 1 at its pinned head; the list may
# shrink when module 1 removes fixtures (an entry whose address is gone is RED, so the list is trimmed in the same change). The residential address the owner's machine had on 2026-07-17 is
# deliberately NOT listed: it is redacted from module 1's current files, and the gate goes red if it ever returns.
# Every entry is a range edge a test probes, a placeholder fixture address, a documented public service, or a version number.
Docs/adr/ADR-0021-smtp-probe-destination-guard.md|*|the ADR names the addresses just outside each blocked range (the boundary cases the probe guard tests use), not hosts
